# Tablet sensors and GPS in Home Assistant (Oct 2026)

Each tablet is its own HA device with environment sensors, RPI-style diagnostics, motion and an opt-in `device_tracker`. RPI (`StudioProjects/RPI`, `data/ha/sensors/*Sensor.kt`) was the reference for which diagnostics to read. RPI sends them through the mobile_app webhook; here they go over the player WebSocket to the add-on, and the integration polls them.

## Wire

- `Protocol.CAPABILITY_TELEMETRY` (`telemetry`): the player lists it in `Hello.capabilities`; the add-on lists it in `PlayerSession.FEATURES`. The player only reports when `Welcome.features` has it **and** it is paired.
- `PlayerMessage.Telemetry(telemetry: DeviceTelemetry)` (`shared/.../DeviceTelemetry.kt`). Every group is optional: `hardware`, `battery`, `network`, `system`, `environment`, `motion`, `location`. `hardware` (`TelemetryHardware`) lists the sensors the tablet has; HA only creates hardware-backed entities for those.
- `ScreenSettings.reportTelemetry` (default **true**) and `shareLocation` (default **false**). HA switches `report_telemetry` / `share_location`; editor checkboxes under **Tablet sensors** in `ScreenPanel.vue` (`reportTelemetry` absent means on).

## Player (`data/device/telemetry/`)

- `TelemetrySource` (interface, bound in `di/TelemetryModule.kt`) → `DeviceTelemetrySource` composes `DiagnosticsReader` (battery, Wi-Fi, storage, memory, versions), `EnvironmentSensorMonitor` (light, pressure, ambient temperature, humidity, proximity), `MotionMonitor` (accelerometer minus low-pass gravity, plus significant-motion trigger; `isMoving` latched 60 s) and `LocationMonitor` (platform `LocationManager`: fused on API 31+, else network, else GPS; 5 min / 50 m). Positions do not use Play Services.
- `TelemetryReporter.update(scope, isEnabled, wantsLocation, send)`: a report at once, then every `REPORT_INTERVAL_MS` (60 s), plus on `changes` (light ±20 % and ≥ 5 lx, proximity flip, motion start, new fix), folded to one per `MIN_REPORT_GAP_MS` (5 s). Snapshots run on the IO dispatcher. Location needs the setting **and** the permission. Each report recomputes that from `wantsLocation && hasLocationPermission()` and calls `LocationMonitor.start()` again while the fix is still null. Do not freeze the share flag for the life of the job: granting permission in Android settings must start sharing without a reconnect. `LocationMonitor` asks for one fix immediately (`getCurrentLocation`, or `requestSingleUpdate` before API 30) because a wall tablet may never move the 50 m that later updates wait for.
- `PlayerViewModel.updateTelemetry()` runs on Welcome, on `reportTelemetry`/`shareLocation` changes, and on the location permission result. Turning location on without permission sends `PlayerEvent.RequestLocationPermission`. The settings dialog offers "Allow location for Home Assistant" only while the kiosk is unlocked (`canOfferLocationPermission`); lock task blocks the system settings screens. The permission dialog itself still fires on the rising edge of sharing.
- Manifest: coarse + fine location (no background location; the player is a foreground kiosk), `uses-feature required=false` for location and each sensor. SSID/BSSID need location permission on Android 8+, so a real Wi-Fi name in HA is proof the permission is granted.

## Location accuracy

- Indoor wall tablets often return no fix from GPS alone. Android's **Location accuracy** (Google Location Accuracy: Wi-Fi and cell) is a separate switch from the app permission and from the device location master switch.
- `LocationAccuracy` / `GoogleLocationAccuracy` (`play-services-location`, bound in `TelemetryModule`): when sharing turns on, a device owner calls `DevicePolicyManager.setLocationEnabled(true)` (API 30+). That does not turn Location accuracy on. There is no device-owner API for it; `content://com.google.settings/partner` (`network_location_opt_in`) needs `WRITE_GSETTINGS`.
- After permission is granted, once per process, `findAccuracyPrompt()` uses `SettingsClient.checkLocationSettings` (`PRIORITY_HIGH_ACCURACY`, `setAlwaysShow(true)`). A `ResolvableApiException` becomes `PlayerEvent.RequestLocationAccuracy`. Already-on accuracy returns null and shows nothing. Declining toasts `location_accuracy_denied`. Call `findAccuracyPrompt()` from the main thread.
- A locked kiosk would block that Play Services screen. `KioskManager.setLocationAccuracyDialogAllowed(true)` adds `com.google.android.gms` to the lock-task packages only while the prompt is up, then restores the player package. `onLocationAccuracyResult` always restores the list.

## Add-on

- `PlayerSession.telemetry` / `telemetryAt` hold the last report (memory only; gone when the tablet disconnects). `PlayerStatus` adds `charging`, `wifi`, `telemetry`, `telemetryAt`.
- `GET /integration/players` returns every `PlayerStatus`, including tablets with no screen. `/integration/screens` is unchanged.

## Integration

- `coordinator.data` is still screens by id; `coordinator.players` is tablets by device id. An add-on without `/players` (404 → `RemoteScreensNotFoundError`) falls back to the players embedded in screens.
- Tablet device: identifier `(DOMAIN, "player_<deviceId>")`, `via_device` the screen. `__init__` registers screen devices before platforms load so `via_device` always exists. Service targets map a tablet device to its `screenId`.
- `RemoteScreensTabletEntity` is unavailable while the tablet is offline, except the `online` binary sensor.
- Entities are added once a tablet is online and reports telemetry (battery, kiosk, online, charging and awake also work for older players). The `device_tracker` is created only after `telemetry.location` exists, on the tablet device (not the screen). It shows on the Map once it has a state.
- Names and enum states in `strings.json`; copy it to `translations/en.json`.

## Gotchas

- Motion relies on the 60 s latch because HA polls every 30 s. A real-time push (`remote_screens_tablet_moved` event) is out of scope for now.
- `BatteryManager.BATTERY_PLUGGED_DOCK` is API 33; `DiagnosticsReader` uses its value (8) as a constant. Cycle count reads `android.os.extra.CYCLE_COUNT` on API 34+.
- `TelemetryReporter` restarts only when the effective location sharing changes, so repeated `Settings` messages do not reset the schedule. The share flag is still recomputed on every report.
- A null `location` group with a visible Wi-Fi SSID means permission is granted and sharing may be on, but Android has not returned a fix. Check Location accuracy before changing `LocationMonitor`.
- Proximity on the PX30 office keypad (STK3A5X, `sensors.rk30board.so`) advertises a 9 cm binary range but emits `0` for far and `1` for near. `ProximityScale` reads that index; `distance < maximumRange` stays on forever. A 9 cm sensor that actually reports 9 cm for far is left on the Android comparison after that sample.

